{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen shared test-support files contain audited repetition, history, measurements, or duplicated explanation. The scope is revalidated on `origin/main` at `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`; `_nested_pytest.py` anchors are refreshed for current code.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only these blocks: `_bank_observer.py:1-34,49-60,83-96,124-134`; `_child_diag.py:56-84,97-118`; `_extra_guard.py:1-23`; `_git_counts.py:1-13`; `_git_floor.py:1-16`; `_git_upkeep.py:1-46`; `_isolation.py:22-29,33-46,122-131,145-156,176-184`; `_jira_shape_contract.py:1-19`; `_live_jira_confinement.py:1-23`; `_log_integrity.py:1-44,104-113`; `_nested_pytest.py:1-23,54-69`; `_repo_root.py:1-21`; `_stall_remote.py:1-12`; `_subprocess_isolation.py:1-28`; `_topology_template.py:212-226`; `_tree_scan.py:1-10`; `conftest.py:1-20,137-142,149-156,196-205,229-245,272-282,289-298,388-400,404-410,444-457,504-515,538-550,556-579,587-597,619-632,639-656,739-755,779-814`; and `module_size_support.py:1-18`. Preserve all other text, non-docstring AST, runtime strings, assertions, and directives.\n\n## Scope\n- Bank/diagnostic helpers — Preserve signature-faithful forwarding, seeded-write exclusion, actor-agnostic first durable banks, distinct executed responses, notice exclusion/fallback, bounded terminal oracle; return-code-before-traceback diagnostics, default/explicit acceptable codes, negative-signal-only rejection, accepted positive `128+N`, shared tails, and length bounds.\n- Extra/git helpers — Preserve lean-install skip versus `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1` error, unaffected binary/version skips; retry rules for nonzero/empty git samples and terminal diagnostics; single-sourced Git floor and fail-before-marker behavior; exact upkeep pins before push, positive trace, and detached-maintenance refusal.\n- Isolation/Jira/log helpers — Preserve bounded timeout-only sampling without sleep, non-attributing/nondeleting diagnostics and destructive-warning order; value-agnostic shared Jira shape oracle; exact live-Jira xdist confinement predicate; logger roots, propagation failure/restoration, per-test level containment, and movement reporting.\n- Nested pytest/repo/network helpers — Preserve caller-owned basetemp, exact env forwarding, parent creation, optional cache suppression, timeout propagation, no `check`, unchanged `CompletedProcess`, intentional exceptions, and all detected launch forms; cached dual-marker repo-root discovery; no-body stall versus rate-progress dribble with caller shutdown.\n- Scan/topology/size helpers — Preserve import-aware hazard classification and nonblank opt-outs; all contained bare-repo pin checks before copy; resolved, sorted, immutable one-parse tree scans; newline/surrogateescape module-size counting, cache exclusion, POSIX keys, and import stability.\n- `conftest.py` — Preserve pytest hook/fixture semantics: extra/floor ordering, external/platform confinement, `UsageError` diagnostics, framework exemptions, report-only isolation, review-bot exit neutralization, environment precedence, repo guards, and logger restoration.\n\nConsumers are pytest itself plus the e2e, integration, interface, external, policy, module-size, and reconciliation tests that import these helpers. No targeted block has an argparse/autodoc/`__doc__` consumer. Preserve the complete ordered directive-line inventory (`noqa`, `type: ignore`, `pragma: no cover`, pyright/mypy/ruff/fmt/isort) exactly.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only comments/true docstrings or blank lines in the declared, reviewed blocks; non-docstring AST, runtime strings, assertions, and exact directives remain unchanged.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the remediation posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: path/block, pinned before citation, final-commit after citation (or DELETED plus neighbor), preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, semantic-preservation verdict, bloat-removal verdict, and reviewer session.\n- [ ] Every row has `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; bloat removal requires shorter text with repetition/history/ornament removed rather than relocated.\n- [ ] Recorded focused checks, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n- [ ] Missing or FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded normalized AST/directive guard, focused tests, diff check, and `make verify`. The independent TSV judges prose quality."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788611711319982001,"uuid":"ca3a09f6-552d-48cc-968e-4bc8471e6fc1"}